{"title":"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Apollonius)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Apollonius)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Median_length_formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Median length formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(AM-GM_Inequality)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (AM-GM Inequality)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Cheese_(Barely_Any_Risk_and_So_Much_Easier))\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Cheese (Barely Any Risk and So Much Easier))</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are points in the plane with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2913c8dfbf0acf66a31c49b621e09698af2bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/93241a11d852322f259dc6088df74d75ee63048a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the length of the line segment from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Define a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> by letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> be the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Then the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is an open interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b7a40ab0d8178e83fe1b91c511d04b1246059b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and the maximum value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/e/63e54fb61882c15b4a1e5dedefbdba511b0b0fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"10\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fe4726ba705cea35c5c6479796aa9ac6acd79cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r+s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e0027e8f1d061b677a650192ad56f7f44a360548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }909\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }910\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }911\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }912\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }913\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"479\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and let the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6dab5ea284b6fc34b0d0ac826edf869cbe0c479f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM = CM = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"14\" />. We know there are limits to the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and these limits can probably be found through the triangle inequality. But the triangle inequality relates the third side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and doesn't contain any information about the median. Therefore we're going to have to write the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and then use the triangle inequality to find bounds on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>We use Stewart's theorem to relate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to the median <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d2f058d4b17a22aa3ecd267c11c1645e3bd73a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$man + dad = bmb + cnc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" />. In this case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c2f6b59d3cefc4f36fb181e8f163805e84955d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{a}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de7ea92c09feafc9680a6704ec0a2eb4deff252.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\frac{a}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"34\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/7257e26071cf0f382f6c2baa0369b9c14fac2a30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c562397c4a8baff106ef9127bdc06839b79a5e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be568a4aecdf30ece7952d5fedd223349794277f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10909493a0b1cbd401cf8397301953bb87acdad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore we get the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9063a1664f3c38007a1ffd765a87fd652cbaf929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^3 + 2ax^2 = a \\cdot 42^2 + a \\cdot 40^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e0014d94d129a33b5b4474346143d9753b076f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^2 + 2x^2 = 42^2 + 40^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc422520580d848c30daca336cc39b89de733443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-21-29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> is a pythagorean triple, this means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d8840ce5992504160fc2a4165f72e65addd76c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^2 + 2x^2 = 58^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0c1e49562e89dd7efac1d34718b22a30453ccef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies a^2 = \\frac{58^2}{2}-x^2\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f40ac18f4f353fa07dd361368cc3f19d0220eb55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies a = \\sqrt{\\frac{58^2}{2}-x^2}\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>By triangle inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/9/199184fa1fcbdaaf463c7e8bd2bc7a0ff6e90468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+40&gt;42 \\implies a&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d9a692e802ac7e242ab17fb96f57ef75309ef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40+42&gt;2a \\implies a&lt;41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"205\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Let's tackle the first inequality: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f10298b433308bb840752e469de08227e20a03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{58^2}{2}-x^2}&gt;1 \\implies x^2 &lt; \\frac{58^2}{2}-1\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e7536c20a846c7f3d0e923d193b9c2391ca5950.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies x^2 &lt; \\frac{40^2+42^2}{2}-1 \\implies x^2&lt;41^2\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Here we use the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f56c35da039f454b1bdc9c24a7226aedb9190533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x^2+(x+2)^2}{2}-1 = (x+1)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"228\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore in this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76daf38f4b429d10e3034c3828f9304aa3fd7541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>For the second inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f122adb32fd296223971814ca21a083f19ad43e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{58^2}{2}-x^2} &lt; 41 \\implies x^2 &gt; \\frac{58^2}{2}-41^2\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0f158a30434bc5759ce7c0af22b4e8b9fb1e25.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies x^2 &gt; \\frac{58^2}{2}-1 + 1 - 41^2\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594515473fcf699e34a3d1e7ff1f16232fce33db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies x^2 &gt; 41^2 + 1 - 41^2 \\implies x^2 &gt; 1 \\implies x &gt; 1\\]\" width=\"378\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Therefore we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/6609da4aec42f0be41a466d606536e73968808f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;x&lt;41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />, so the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a89f7b01bd36bd2d98c6d4f3d9e3d419be755f99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,41)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe area of this triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6bec6cbbc70b58f39c8629c3eb6e65586550ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} 42 \\cdot 40 \\cdot \\sin(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"123\" height=\"38\" />. The maximum value of the area occurs when the triangle is right, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1dd299fcc16d94c2710efcc999e6d56fbaeb1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />. Then the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04352cecdeeaa3fcd7b23b071b07d9097a9635e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 40 \\cdot 42 = 840$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"129\" height=\"38\" />. The length of the median of a right triangle is half the length of it's hypotenuse, which squared is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39e18050a7b24a07858bbe64a13bd29e24e6dc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^2+42^2 = 58^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />. Thus the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/a/baaa7ef852915930d8363ad18292069401126f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+41+840+29 = \\boxed{\\textbf{911 } (C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"240\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~KingRavi\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Geometry)\">Solution 2 (Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_amc_12B_P20.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b2/2024_amc_12B_P20.PNG/300px-2024_amc_12B_P20.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"359\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/b2/2024_amc_12B_P20.PNG/450px-2024_amc_12B_P20.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/b2/2024_amc_12B_P20.PNG 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><br />\nLet midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, extends <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31fb34078ad18b2f0e65d3ee7e485ee89effc38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD=x$\" width=\"69\" height=\"12\" />, \n</p><p>triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />  has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd572ce2a4934c684e17ee95679de75039cd3ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(40,42,2x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> , based on triangle inequality,  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7b0256e253c9c913baf9d2e1c087d14bc2d5304.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[42 - 40 &lt;  2x &lt; 42 + 40\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"13\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c20bc71e997ae260507090e0f59cb82c21392943.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 &lt; x  &lt; 41\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be1f3d176d63328e97c2914cc764a2231b461f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p = 1, q=41\\]\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6ea1bda17f717c2bfee80fb5ca61814faa5baef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\cdot f(x) =   40 \\cdot 42 \\cdot \\sin(A) \\le 2\\cdot840\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"18\" /> \nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a83e185dd29f007d0f414541877eb93075cb04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 840$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />\nwhich is achieved when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/55570a457e076e024977c41eff257fa1c2a2edb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" /> , then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c577428f8c7d5deaaf8eefe8641b36af2b281d05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACD = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f25b3b06e55de62d28714cdc044617950cc62a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(2x)^2 = 40^2 + 42^2\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/f/7bf275207f89aa0f77a5c0090ca9e8ee2e938ac0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 29\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca90f61b155648e1b1669ca4e72821f2c8bf0356.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s= 29\\]\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0726463ce21647893e19011787dc28db279a6f47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p+q+s+r = 1 + 41 + 29 + 840 = \\fbox{\\textbf{(C) } 911}\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Trigonometry)\">Solution 3 (Trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let A = (0, 0) , B =(b, 0) , C= (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f3794aa18c3dac9fb1ef5e4c8b1784d96b3b0c91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\cos\\theta , c\\sin\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/623b2d9d5ac588cbcadccdfad131ee3626d1b0c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M = \\left(\\frac{b + c\\cos\\theta}{2}, \\frac{c\\sin\\theta}{2}\\right).\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a02a058664accbae42786aad8e7c52e8f9897325.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AM = x = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{b + c\\cos\\theta}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{c\\sin\\theta}{2}\\right)^2} =  \\frac{\\sqrt{c^2 + 2bc\\cos\\theta+b^2}}{2}.\\]\" width=\"515\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/798b67adf442b76e67316f8208af946aa8b2b587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1d456f8e9e0ec870adaca1bb5331f9b8df5ea31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{\\sqrt{(c+b)^2}}{2} = \\frac{c+b}{2} = \\frac{42+40}{2} = 41.\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da6fb05e09530dc5cc36e2b3da2819ee37e19f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d49b58147c822fe959ca93316a4d0cc097b1d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{\\sqrt{(c-b)^2}}{2} = \\frac{c-b}{2} = \\frac{42-40}{2} = 1.\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"41\" />\nThe domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is the open interval:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f434b1825e40eff30e60a8e470b1ca13ec5f3a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{(1, 41)}.\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>The rest follows Solution 2\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Apollonius.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Apollonius)\">Solution 4 (Apollonius)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Apollonius)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Here's a faster way to solve this problem using Apollonius's Theorem (which is a special case of Stewart's Theorem for medians). In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3271cfad09428436ceeb476cae6d5307470c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${x}^2= \\frac{1}{4}*(2{AB}^2+2{AC}^2-{BC}^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"259\" height=\"38\" />. \nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8ffd7c96b89accffd64b623c867d711637ce52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=1682-\\frac{1}{4}*{BC}^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"174\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\nWe know that, by the Triangle Inequality, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e59ecb22c2acd5cbe6f95c9585e0255b1440677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2&lt;BC&lt;82$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />. Applying these to Apollonius, we have that the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and the maximum value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf9e11afc1ac6cf7dcaadcb301b9f6b27305d5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> (both cannot be reached, however). \n</p><p><br />\nThe rest of the solution follows Solution 1.\n</p><p><br />\n~xHypotenuse\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Median_length_formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Median_length_formula)\">Solution 5 (Median length formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Median length formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Then, by the Median Length Formula:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/682f2acace960b48cb0762691c49c8f6f8aa345d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2*AD^2 = AB^2 - BD^2 + AC^2 - CD^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />.\nIf we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d53112c16ca239cbf4275741f9f5b93f709cdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc975a5b35343ca18565b3a7cce9827d332bbbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />, then we get the relationship that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/4625a60d7db06217a556783d6b8b72520bbcfda6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{1682-n^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"21\" />.\nBy the Triangle Inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f679db7c3f172cd09d3fd3baff5b9e45caf2bf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 &lt; BC &lt; 82$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b32c62d016dd9cde4e1c9c0b7e9d2d77e4bdcf4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; n &lt; 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />. \nThis means that the domain of x is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/13913a71eaa0107ebc20102d30c34db73f783580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{1}, \\sqrt{1681}) = (1, 41)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>The rest follows Solution 1.\n</p><p>~mathwizard123123\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28AM-GM_Inequality.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(AM-GM_Inequality)\">Solution 6 (AM-GM Inequality)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (AM-GM Inequality)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By letting BC equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1c5d8b75d562382fe7092af4b1e8bcd1b648116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, we can use Heron's formula to calculate the area. Notice the semi-perimeter is just\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594a911f944d8727c17c22c14df883bc9aace47c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{40 + 42 + 2a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" /> which is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5ba24b1eedd6d054b8f81acb8f30e8c273b792d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a + 41}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. Next, by Heron's formula, the area of ABC is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d8a8a97e6d0e5b8fd85bd3a2cb7feadd6f7907f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(a + 41)(a + 1)(a - 1)(41 - a)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"258\" height=\"35\" /> which simplifies to the\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46298afddf6d04ee7735556fbdef3547dd6c58e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(a^2 - 1)(41^2 - a^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"35\" />.\nWe now know that the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32f718e6941e582485724ed60f7a91e96c8cc18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${f(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is just the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46298afddf6d04ee7735556fbdef3547dd6c58e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(a^2 - 1)(41^2 - a^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"35\" />. This domain is very easy to calculate. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/586f12656051b7e54516f74bebbf9a07f1811f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} &gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />1 and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c046c583de20239cfeae9ed1e42700925e16b650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} &lt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8e5e9bc5597202a67416e0c7e76a2a882045a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />.\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0d99bcaeae618f28e7a8897b808e8616ec179dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is always positive, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0d99bcaeae618f28e7a8897b808e8616ec179dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is in the open interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b06919200dd276df2c3594fd2c867980c9a5836f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${(1, 41)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />. Now, we find the maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32f718e6941e582485724ed60f7a91e96c8cc18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${f(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />. By the AM-GM inequality, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb33f5f1bf347c276712440e6358b55685745f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{((a^2 - 1) + (41^2 - a^2))}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"184\" height=\"41\" /> ≥ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46298afddf6d04ee7735556fbdef3547dd6c58e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(a^2 - 1)(41^2 - a^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"35\" />. Simplifying and letting\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46298afddf6d04ee7735556fbdef3547dd6c58e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(a^2 - 1)(41^2 - a^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"35\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32f718e6941e582485724ed60f7a91e96c8cc18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${f(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32f718e6941e582485724ed60f7a91e96c8cc18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${f(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> ≤ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35a8322117e518a8721875997da35deb6039d2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{41^2 - 1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"63\" height=\"41\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331c19dee39fa5dc2c47298bff8327c13b0e8918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${840}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. We know by AM-GM that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c32f718e6941e582485724ed60f7a91e96c8cc18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${f(x)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331c19dee39fa5dc2c47298bff8327c13b0e8918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${840}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0a3a9375865e1855b52ba296600fb87e9b2968.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} -$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />1 = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/1130b649fba5f62426f86eff6efa817dc9b80ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41^{2}  -$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373f3e9c1a9cba15c65e133604eb42156015afe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. Solving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0d99bcaeae618f28e7a8897b808e8616ec179dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a25a7b0d3b1f3a9421a10d6c6f21814288dc5ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, we have found the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/18918c61e6a0b18353c19002b5810e9afeaadaf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${f}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is the open interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b06919200dd276df2c3594fd2c867980c9a5836f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${(1, 41)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> and the maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/18918c61e6a0b18353c19002b5810e9afeaadaf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${f}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/331c19dee39fa5dc2c47298bff8327c13b0e8918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${840}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> which occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f64c96395619031dbe5b637faeb4c1fe609bd56c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${x}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a25a7b0d3b1f3a9421a10d6c6f21814288dc5ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />(Apply Stewart's to triangle ABC when knowing that BC = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f1fd78ac2167988ec5b1f9f1f04196600dd0b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${58}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.) Adding these up, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f47ed1a71cff1c834f1d5a347f8f873217cf2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1 + 41 + 840 + 29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a04f7594d0b80ecf11600fd62befd0cf84fa047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${911}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Cheese_.28Barely_Any_Risk_and_So_Much_Easier.29.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Cheese_(Barely_Any_Risk_and_So_Much_Easier))\">Solution 7 (Cheese (Barely Any Risk and So Much Easier))</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Cheese (Barely Any Risk and So Much Easier))\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can easily see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1f3fb4b8cff3eb5cf276509696f29b8081e4f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Dom}(f)=(1, 41)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> by considering extreme cases of degenerate triangles (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />). Then, the maximum area is extremely likely to be when the triangle is right, which happens when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde583eb50948f471b722e1ca6c213ce39c12305.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc422520580d848c30daca336cc39b89de733443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-21-29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangle, but scaled up). The area of this triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd39493493659fb36ab2875b266a4874b475f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$840$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a1c88eb804cbc06c4f5e6c0346056e83fbcb110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40 \\approx 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />, the median length is approximately equal to the altitude length, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f50873682b493ef05c4c5ff48a2c570557462f81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1680}{58}=\\frac{840}{29}=\\frac{870-30}{29}=30-\\frac{30}{29} \\approx 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"323\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94b96374e6a7a16dcacf8dcbfb7bc46a62105e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+41+840+29= \\boxed{(\\text{C}) \\; 911}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"235\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~scjh999999\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aDajQGay0TQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aDajQGay0TQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B\">2024 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018025258\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.073 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.098 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 884/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28187/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.071      1 -total\n 58.67%    7.669      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.89%    5.084      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:29751:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018025258 and revision id 268467. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}